  "id": "SOFT-HUB-20261024-001-D001",
  "scope_id": "SOFT-HUB-20261024-001",
  "title": "Native emergence cannot imitate a hub exactly, and on trees not approximately",
  "subject": "Whether gadgets without hubs can approximate a hub, for every knot",
  "conclusion": "No native gadget of any knot is an exact hub, and pairs of solutions that do not link all three terminals reroute onto off-diagonal values, which bounds the hub ratio of windable gadgets by the square root of 3 (given McQuillan) and of parity and no-lone gadgets by 1. For the six open knots, tree gadgets are proved to have hub ratio at most 3; gadgets with cycles remain a conjecture.",
